  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INTEGRATED WATERSHED MNGMT FOR MEXICANOS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project implements part of the Mexicanos Lagoon Watershed Management Plan developed under a prior NAWCA grant .This phase will: 1) restore (810.16) acres of wetlands in Mexicanos Lagoon, (498.94) acres of wetlands in Bustillos lagoon, (64.22) acres of uplands adjacent to Mexicanos Lagoon, and (158.08) acres of uplands adjacent to Bustillos Lagoon; 2) protect 118.56 acres adjacent to Mexicanos lagoon and 1,605.5 acres adjacent to Bustillos Lagoon; 3) educate and train 180 people from communities in the Mexicanos and Bustillos watersheds through environmental education workshops and workshops on low environmental impact agricultural and ranching practices; 4) monitor wetlands productivity as well as habitat use by waterfowl, shorebirds, and other waterbirds; and 5) develop a public involvement program targeting the conservation of Mexicanos and Bustillos Lagoons.</narrative>
  </description>
